# Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in. .env.local is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GITHUB_TOKEN  (optional locally, strongly recommended in CI)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The build fetches every figure the site displays from the public GitHub API.
# Unauthenticated, that is limited to 60 REST requests an hour and 10 search
# requests a minute, counted PER IP ADDRESS. Shared CI runners exhaust it
# routinely, and the build then falls back to the committed data/stats.json.
#
# A token moves you onto your own budget: 5,000 requests an hour.
#
# This token needs NO SCOPES AND NO PERMISSIONS. Every endpoint used is public
# and the token exists only to identify you to the rate limiter.
#
# Create one at:
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
#   → Generate new token → fine-grained
#   → Repository access: Public repositories (read-only)
#   → Permissions: leave every single one unset
#
# Full guide, including how to diagnose a failure:
#   docs/github-api.md
#
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL  (recommended in production)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The origin canonical and Open Graph URLs resolve against. Getting this wrong
# fails silently: og:image resolves to the wrong host and every shared link
# renders a broken preview with no error anywhere.
#
# Defaults to https://aryanghai.in when unset.
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
